overnance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Ardelyx, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $777M market cap on $407M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +98% over the past three years and +33% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -378% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 82% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $44M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -2.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 12% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 3.0% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 10% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 59/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may refl